      <span class="eyebrow">What It Is</span>
      <h2 id="what-heading">Fixed Teeth on Four to Six Implants</h2>
      <span class="gold-rule"></span>
      <p>Full-arch implant treatment uses a small number of strategically placed implants — typically four to six — to support an entire arch of fixed teeth. The prosthesis is screwed into place and stays there. You brush and care for it like natural teeth.</p>
      <p>For many patients, a provisional set of teeth can be placed the same day as the implant surgery. Final restorations are seated once osseointegration — the natural fusion of implant to bone — is complete.</p>
    </div>
